  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "past simple: was/were",
      "title_form": "Pasado simple: was/were",
      "title_target": "Past simple: was/were",
      "description_md_form": "El **pasado simple** de *to be* (ser/estar) tiene solo dos formas: **was** y **were**. Usamos **was** con *I, he, she, it* y **were** con *you, we, they*.\n\n**Afirmativo:**\n- *I was busy.* (Estaba ocupado.)\n- *They were happy.* (Estaban felices.)\n\n**Negativo:** agregamos *not*: *was not* (wasn't) y *were not* (weren't).\n- *The celebration was not boring.* (La celebración no fue aburrida.)\n\n**Preguntas:** invertimos el orden: *Was she nervous?* (¿Estaba ella nerviosa?)\n\n**Uso clave:** lo usamos para describir estados, emociones y situaciones en el pasado, a menudo con *during* (durante) o *as soon as* (tan pronto como).\n\n| Pronombre | Afirmativo | Negativo |\n|-----------|------------|----------|\n| I | was | was not (wasn't) |\n| He/She/It | was | was not (wasn't) |\n| You/We/They | were | were not (weren't) |\n\nAsí puedes cerrar una descripción breve: *I was busy, but I was happy.*",
      "description_md_target": "The **past simple** of *to be* has only two forms: **was** and **were**. We use **was** with *I, he, she, it* and **were** with *you, we, they*.\n\n**Affirmative:**\n- *I was busy.*\n- *They were happy.*\n\n**Negative:** add *not*: *was not* (wasn't) and *were not* (weren't).\n- *The celebration was not boring.*\n\n**Questions:** invert the order: *Was she nervous?*\n\n**Key use:** we use it to describe states, emotions and situations in the past, often with *during* or *as soon as*.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + was/were + complement",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "past_simple_to_be",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Negativo",
          "Pregunta"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "was",
            "was not (wasn't)",
            "Was I...?"
          ],
          [
            "He/She/It",
            "was",
            "was not (wasn't)",
            "Was he/she/it...?"
          ],
          [
            "You",
            "were",
            "were not (weren't)",
            "Were you...?"
          ],
          [
            "We",
            "were",
            "were not (weren't)",
            "Were we...?"
          ],
          [
            "They",
            "were",
            "were not (weren't)",
            "Were they...?"
          ]
        ]
      },
