      "callouts": [
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "text_md": "**Tip:** *was* y *were* son las únicas formas del pasado de *to be*. No necesitas otra palabra para el pasado: *I was busy* ya significa \"estuve/estaba ocupado\"."
        },
        {
          "type": "common_error",
          "text_md": "**Error común:** no digas *I were* o *she were*. Con *I, he, she, it* siempre usamos **was**: *I was busy*, *she was nervous*."
        },
        {
          "type": "warning",
          "text_md": "**Cuidado:** en preguntas, el verbo va primero: *Was she surprised?* No digas *She was surprised?* (eso es solo para confirmar con entonación)."
        }
      ],
      "common_errors_es": [
        "Usar *were* con *I*: ✗ *I were busy* → ✓ *I was busy*.",
        "Olvidar el verbo en preguntas: ✗ *You were nervous?* → ✓ *Were you nervous?*",
        "Confundir *was* con *is* en pasado: ✗ *Yesterday I is busy* → ✓ *Yesterday I was busy*.",
        "Poner *did* con *to be*: ✗ *Did you be happy?* → ✓ *Were you happy?*"
      ]
    }
  ],
